  "_left_as_counts_only": {
    "_why": [
      "Assessed and deliberately NOT given a membership pin. For each, the count",
      "guards what it can (the module still collects, the selection still selects)",
      "and a membership pin would add nothing the module does not already enforce",
      "on itself, or would pin a subject that is not a refusal."
    ],
    "substrate-proofs": "test_substrate / test_opened_substrate / test_mount_relevance / test_mount_root_formats are host-fact taxonomies. Their property is that a mount classification is TOTAL over the observed shapes, and each module already asserts that totality internally (an unclassified shape fails inside the module, not by being absent from a list here). A CI name list would restate a guard the module keeps on itself.",
    "attestation-proofs": "test_config_attestation (87) is a digest/encoding module. Its membership property -- that every posture field is in the digest -- is enforced by its own POSTURE_FIELDS agreement test, which fails if a field is added and left out. That is a stronger check than naming tests here, and it lives where the field is added.",
    "prod-fix-1": "test_approval_expiry_across_preparation / test_attestation_chronology / test_unicode_hostname_taxonomy are boundary sweeps over generated inputs. Their composition is the input space, not the test names, and the input space is pinned in the modules.",
    "prod-fix-2": "test_secret_canary_sweep discovers credential-shaped fields FROM THE DATACLASS and fails if one is unswept. Membership is derived from the source, not from a list, which is the property this whole file is arguing for -- there is nothing to pin here that the sweep does not already derive.",
    "composed-message-proofs": "Already pins five required names inline, in the step, since G13. Left where it is rather than moved here: it is the pattern this file generalises, and relocating it would churn a working guard for symmetry alone."
  }
}
